{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Molecular.co2_lp_dual_binding","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Molecular.co2_lp_dual_binding","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Order.Defs.PartialOrder","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum"],"declarations":27,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.co2_lp_dual_binding","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.co2_lp_dual_binding","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/co2_lp_dual_binding.lean#L149-L168","doc":"**Theorem (conditional on `Co2SymmetricSelection`)** — the resolving\ndeclaration for `lean.ref` `qou:QOU.Molecular.co2_lp_dual_binding`.\n\nConjoins (1) the *derived* carbon-valence feasibility\n`k₁ + k₂ ≤ 4` of the symmetric candidate, (2) the *derived* strand\ncount `n_strands = 66`, and (3) the *derived*\nsymmetric-beats-asymmetric inequalities\n`Φ₁(2,2) ≤ Φ₁(3,1)` and `Φ₁(2,2) ≤ Φ₁(1,3)`.  Every conjunct is\nderived; the conjectural LP-dual selection enters only as the\nquantified `symmetric_minimises` hypothesis. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:co2-lp-dual-binding","label":"prop:co2-lp-dual-binding","md":"quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/co2-lp-dual-binding.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.co2_symmetric_beats_asymmetric","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.co2_symmetric_beats_asymmetric","kind":"theorem","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/co2_lp_dual_binding.lean#L133-L147","doc":"**Theorem (conditional on `Co2SymmetricSelection`)** — the symmetric\ndouble-bond configuration `(2,2)` has `Φ₁` no greater than either\nasymmetric alternative `(3,1)` or `(1,3)`.\n\nDerived (not projected): instantiate the minimisation *hypothesis*\nat `c = asym31` and `c = asym13`.  New inequalities on `Φ₁` values,\nobtained by using the quantified hypothesis at two points. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.co2_strand_count","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.co2_strand_count","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/co2_lp_dual_binding.lean#L125-L131","doc":"**CO₂ strand count — derived sorry-free.**  The molecular braid\nuses `18 + 2·24 = 66` strands, evaluated from the per-atom\ncomposition inputs — not a projected definitional field. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.co2_carbon_valence_feasible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.co2_carbon_valence_feasible","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/co2_lp_dual_binding.lean#L115-L123","doc":"**Carbon-valence feasibility of the symmetric candidate — derived\nsorry-free.**  The symmetric double-bond configuration satisfies\ncarbon's valence constraint: `k₁ + k₂ = 2 + 2 ≤ 4`.  The LP\nprimal-feasibility check, computed from the definitional geometry\ninputs — not a projected hypothesis field. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.Co2SymmetricSelection.symmetric_minimises","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.Co2SymmetricSelection.symmetric_minimises","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/co2_lp_dual_binding.lean#L112-L112","doc":"The symmetric configuration minimises `Φ₁` over all feasible\nconfigurations (the ground-state selection hypothesis). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.Co2SymmetricSelection.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.Co2SymmetricSelection.mk","kind":"ctor","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/co2_lp_dual_binding.lean#L109-L109","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.Co2SymmetricSelection","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.Co2SymmetricSelection","kind":"class","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/co2_lp_dual_binding.lean#L104-L113","doc":"§3b-cond conjecture class (non-degenerate per AGENTS.md §3b-cond\nitem 5): carries the conjectural LP-dual *hypothesis* — the\nsymmetric `(2,2)` configuration is the `Φ₁`-minimiser over all\ncarbon-valence-feasible configurations — as a quantified field, NOT\nany conclusion of the theorems below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.Co2LpDualBindingContext.Phi1_config","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.Co2LpDualBindingContext.Phi1_config","kind":"def","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/co2_lp_dual_binding.lean#L102-L102","doc":"`Φ₁` of each carbon-valence-feasible bond configuration. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.Co2LpDualBindingContext.n_strands_def","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.Co2LpDualBindingContext.n_strands_def","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/co2_lp_dual_binding.lean#L100-L100","doc":"The molecular strand count is the carbon contribution plus two\noxygen contributions (definitional composition input). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.Co2LpDualBindingContext.n_strands","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.Co2LpDualBindingContext.n_strands","kind":"def","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/co2_lp_dual_binding.lean#L97-L97","doc":"The number of strands in the CO₂ molecular braid. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.Co2LpDualBindingContext.strands_O_def","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.Co2LpDualBindingContext.strands_O_def","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/co2_lp_dual_binding.lean#L95-L95","doc":"Each oxygen contributes `8 + 8 + 8 = 24` strands. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.Co2LpDualBindingContext.strands_O","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.Co2LpDualBindingContext.strands_O","kind":"def","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/co2_lp_dual_binding.lean#L93-L93","doc":"Strand count contributed by each oxygen atom: 8 protons +\n8 neutrons + 8 electrons (definitional composition input). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.Co2LpDualBindingContext.strands_C_def","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.Co2LpDualBindingContext.strands_C_def","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/co2_lp_dual_binding.lean#L90-L90","doc":"Carbon contributes `6 + 6 + 6 = 18` strands. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.Co2LpDualBindingContext.strands_C","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.Co2LpDualBindingContext.strands_C","kind":"def","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/co2_lp_dual_binding.lean#L88-L88","doc":"Strand count contributed by the carbon atom: 6 protons +\n6 neutrons + 6 electrons (definitional composition input). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.Co2LpDualBindingContext.k2_def","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.Co2LpDualBindingContext.k2_def","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/co2_lp_dual_binding.lean#L85-L85","doc":"The symmetric candidate places a double bond to the second oxygen\n(definitional geometry input). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.Co2LpDualBindingContext.k1_def","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.Co2LpDualBindingContext.k1_def","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/co2_lp_dual_binding.lean#L82-L82","doc":"The symmetric candidate places a double bond to the first oxygen\n(definitional geometry input). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.Co2LpDualBindingContext.k2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.Co2LpDualBindingContext.k2","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/co2_lp_dual_binding.lean#L79-L79","doc":"Bond order to the second oxygen atom in the symmetric candidate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.Co2LpDualBindingContext.k1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.Co2LpDualBindingContext.k1","kind":"def","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/co2_lp_dual_binding.lean#L77-L77","doc":"Bond order to the first oxygen atom in the symmetric candidate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.Co2LpDualBindingContext.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.Co2LpDualBindingContext.mk","kind":"ctor","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/co2_lp_dual_binding.lean#L75-L75","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.Co2LpDualBindingContext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.Co2LpDualBindingContext","kind":"class","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/co2_lp_dual_binding.lean#L72-L102","doc":"Data of the CO₂ LP-dual-binding claim. All fields are *inputs*\n(the symmetric candidate's bond orders, the molecular composition,\nand the `Φ₁`-functional); none is a conclusion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.instDecidableEqCo2Config","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.instDecidableEqCo2Config","kind":"instance","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/co2_lp_dual_binding.lean#L70-L70","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.Co2Config.asym04","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.Co2Config.asym04","kind":"ctor","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/co2_lp_dual_binding.lean#L69-L69","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.Co2Config.asym40","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.Co2Config.asym40","kind":"ctor","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/co2_lp_dual_binding.lean#L68-L68","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.Co2Config.asym13","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.Co2Config.asym13","kind":"ctor","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/co2_lp_dual_binding.lean#L67-L67","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.Co2Config.asym31","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.Co2Config.asym31","kind":"ctor","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/co2_lp_dual_binding.lean#L66-L66","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.Co2Config.sym","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.Co2Config.sym","kind":"ctor","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/co2_lp_dual_binding.lean#L65-L65","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.Co2Config","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.Co2Config","kind":"inductive","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/co2_lp_dual_binding.lean#L61-L70","doc":"The five carbon-valence-feasible bond configurations\n`(k₁, k₂)` with `k₁ + k₂ ≤ 4`, encoded as an index type.\n`sym` is the symmetric `(2,2)`; `asym31` is `(3,1)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}